line	<str>Head all the way east until you reach a small cave with a chest. Pray melee when you fall down until passing through the metal door 3.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the small cave and pick the lock on the chest. Search the chest and you will obtain a bronze key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Move through the Bronze Door just north-west of this chest. If you must leave and return, you will need to obtain the bronze key again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Move north until checkpoint 4, pray ranged when you fall down. Note: The cave below has many dead ends. Check the map to memorize the route towards the rope (checkpoint 3).</str>
line	
line	<str>Move west to checkpoint 5.</str>
line	
line	<str>Continue reading at the #Combined part section below.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need a slash weapon in order to cut webs, as well as a pickaxe to mine rocks blocking your path. It is not possible to fail slashing a web if that web is on the correct path.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pray ranged all the way until checkpoint 5. You will be attacked by both melee and ranged, but due to distance, melee attacks are less frequent.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>There are several spots where you will stand between climbable rocks and a web. These can be treated as safespots if you ever need to take a rest.</col>
step	44	-	Quick guide step 44
line	<str>Talk to King Narnode Shareen, located in the Gnome Stronghold's Grand tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Glough's house south-east of the Grand Tree and go upstairs, then climb the eastern tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Right click and investigate the tree to receive a handkerchief.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Anita in her house north of the Gnome Ball Field (use north-western-most staircase to get into house).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Glough's house again, go up the tree to the uk=2, then climb again to reach the uk=3. (to reach the uk=3 you must click the northern branch)</str>
line	
line	<str>Investigate the gnome statue and turn it to unlock the cupboard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard for book of spyology, the gnome crates for a brush, and fire remains for mysterious note.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use pestle and mortar on the lemon</str>
line	
line	<str>Use notes on the candles</str>
line	
line	<str>Use pestle and mortar on grapes</str>
line	
line	<str>Use juice-coated brush on mysterious note.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the scrawled note.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to King Narnode. Read the translation book he gives you. (You may already have the translation book from a prerequisite quest: The Grand Tree, if this is the case King Narnode will not hand you a second copy.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Use translation book on the note, and talk to King Narnode again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Anita again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the translated note.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the King again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Assistant Lori next to the hot air balloon beside Glough's house.</str>
line	
line	<str>Fly to Entrana via balloon and talk to Auguste.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the Gnome stronghold and talk to King Narnode again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Ape Atoll (CLR, one of the two Ape Atoll Teleports or via the gliders used in the first quest).</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip your monkey/gorilla greegree and use the agility shortcuts as a monkey to climb the vine down to the village.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Garkor located outside Awowogei's house.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Awowogei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Garkor again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go all the way to the West side of the island and go up the hill to the Monkey Archers.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to a Monkey Archer about Kruk.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the tracks (foot prints) that start at the foot of the hill until you reach a trapdoor ("Jungle Grass") at the foot of a palm tree just north-west of the bamboo gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>(red|Warning: If inventory is full, your greegree will be dropped to the floor upon entering the dungeon.) Go down the trapdoor and go south.</str>
line	
line	<str>Navigate the maze via the agility path to the east or the tank pathway to the south. You will be able to create a shortcut after the maze, allowing for banking. It is very easy to die here if you are not careful and paying attention to which prayers you need to use. Prayer potions and good food are highly recommended for this.</str>
line	
line	<str>It is recommended to consult the map to follow the right route towards the end.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you fail an obstacle and receive a message '...this route feels wrong', you have to take the other path instead.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will come across areas throughout the agility path that contain Dodgy Ground, such as at the start of the path. The trick here is to only walk on the tiles that do NOT appear cracked, since otherwise you will fall down. These are fairly easily distinguishable as the "cracked ground" tiles look as if they have slightly darker cracks in the shape of an "X" on each tile, while the safer tiles look smooth and uncracked.</str>
line	
line	<str>Throughout this path, as soon as you inevitably fall down, you will want to immediately pray either against melee or ranged, respectively, depending on how far you are through the path. Otherwise you can very easily and quickly die. Quickly make your way to whichever hanging vine is available to you, and click it in order to return to the surface of the maze.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head all the way east until you reach a small cave with a chest. Pray melee when you fall down until passing through the metal door 3.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the small cave and pick the lock on the chest. Search the chest and you will obtain a bronze key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Move through the Bronze Door just north-west of this chest. If you must leave and return, you will need to obtain the bronze key again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Move north until checkpoint 4, pray ranged when you fall down. Note: The cave below has many dead ends. Check the map to memorize the route towards the rope (checkpoint 3).</str>
line	
line	<str>Move west to checkpoint 5.</str>
line	
line	<str>Continue reading at the #Combined part section below.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need a slash weapon in order to cut webs, as well as a pickaxe to mine rocks blocking your path. It is not possible to fail slashing a web if that web is on the correct path.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pray ranged all the way until checkpoint 5. You will be attacked by both melee and ranged, but due to distance, melee attacks are less frequent.</str>
line	
line	<str>There are several spots where you will stand between climbable rocks and a web. These can be treated as safespots if you ever need to take a rest.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>If you run into a rock or a web which you're unable to break or cut through, and you get a game message in chat containing something like '...Maybe find another route.', you will have to try another route.</col>
