done	
done	<str>Talk to Garkor.</str>
done	
done	<str>Teleport to Trollheim using standard spellbook teleport or stony basalt and enter the Troll Stronghold.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go south-west of the entrance into the room with Kob.</str>
done	
done	<str>Activate Protect from Melee and talk to Kob.</str>
done	
done	<str>Fight Kob until he gives up.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Kob again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Make your way to Gu'Tanoth. Use the 71 Agility shortcut, or follow the western path to the end.</str>
done	
done	<str>Activate Protect from Melee and talk to Keef. Fight him until he gives up.</str>
done	
done	<str>You may now want to bank your heavy armour and weapons and withdraw your graceful outfit and some stamina potions, as there is no more combat involved in the next section.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go back to Ape Atoll and talk to Garkor near Awowogei.</str>
done	
done	<str>Find Assistant Le Smith and talk to him , who is found somewhere on the rooftops of Marim. There are four possible locations:</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Garkor.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the west side of the island and talk to the monkey guard next to a boat to go to the airship platform.</str>
done	
done	<str>Navigate your way through the maze without being caught by the ninja monkeys. You will need to pick up 6 satchels, fill them with explosives, then use them in 6 different locations. Any explosives that have already been placed will remain even if caught.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go back to the boat, you can get caught to make it faster.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Garkor.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the trapdoor to the dungeon you fought Kruk in.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go north to find monkey bars. Equip your Kruk greegree and use the monkey bars.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the passage into Glough's laboratory.</str>
done	
done	<str>Climb on the stunted demonic gorilla and go down the stairs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Fight the three gorillas until they return to their cages. Use Protect from Melee if necessary.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use Holding area to dismount the stunted demonic gorilla.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the crates for a chisel and hammer if needed.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go upstairs and tamper with the device to the north.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the chisel on the charged onyx, then use the deconstructed onyx on the device.</str>
done	
done	<str>Investigate an incubation chamber.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Garkor.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Awowogei.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Garkor again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to King Narnode in the Grand Tree.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Nieve. If you ever lose Nieve, she will be at the front doors of the Grand Tree.</str>
done	
done	<str>Walk around the Gnome Stronghold, and kill 4 tortured gorillas until Nieve notifies you to find Garkor. (They will only attack with melee and can be safespotted behind various objects)</str>
done	
done	<str>Gear up with 2 attack (combat) styles and go north-west of the Grand Tree to Garkor. (near the swamp toad and king worm swamp and the tortoise enclosure)</str>
done	
done	<str>Leave the gnome stronghold and go north-east, past the tortured gorillas, to enter the cave.</str>
done	
done	<str>Follow the path to Glough.</str>
done	
done	<str>Kill the 2 tortured gorillas and 2 demonic gorillas. It's recommended to kill one tortured gorilla, then the Demonic gorilla that jumps down. Then proceed to kill the other tortured gorilla and demonic gorilla.</str>
done	
done	<str>At this point you can safely teleport out and restock. Glough can hit 66 with his melee attack and 40+ with his ranged attack.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the next room and attack Glough until he moves on to the next room. He can be safespotted in this first room.</str>
done	
done	<str>In this second room, lure Glough back to the first room and hug the north wall two squares past the divot to safespot him with ranged/magic (because praying ranged does not protect you) until he moves on to the next room.</str>
done	
done	<str>In the final room, kill Glough. It is recommended to use protect from melee if you're close to Glough and protect from magic if you're at a distance. He will try to push/pull you depending on your location. (Can be flinched with a bow with an attack range of ten or more. This requires a 10-minute de-aggro.)</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Zooknock and ask him to teleport you to the Grand Tree.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to King Narnode.</str>
done	
done	<col=ff0000>QUEST COMPLETE!</col>
